codex
The direct comprehension executes correctly, but its desugaring allocates two temporary lists per element, which makes the symbolic loop invariant carry an unbounded heap history. I’m replacing it with the equivalent `append` loop supported natively by the reference semantics. This preserves the HumanEval behavior while yielding a stable heap object and a tractable inductive invariant.
